      "body": "【Emotional signature】\nRock Water shows up where self-discipline runs very high and principle matters greatly. You may have set yourself clear rules and standards, holding a long consistency and control — and without noticing, the body has grown rigid. This isn't a lack of warmth. It's a deep investment in an ideal, and flexibility has stepped out of the system for a while.\n【Through the lens of neuroception】\nWhat this card reflects: the body treats \"don't deviate, don't slacken\" as safety, so it holds the structure tightly and avoids any change.\nIn this state, the body may show:\n* Stiffness in the spine or joints; movement without flow\n\n* Strong attachment to rules and principles\n\n* Inner tension rising the moment the plan is departed from\n\nThis is not a problem. The body is keeping order — it just loses its room to breathe.\n【How this essence supports you】\nThe support of Rock Water is in letting some give come back. It doesn't deny discipline or principle. It lets the body slowly feel that flexibility isn't the same as losing control. When softness is allowed in, strength becomes more durable and more able to move.\n【Today's practice】\nSomewhere in the day, find a moment and let your attention rest lightly on your spine or your joints. There's no need to change your posture — just know that the body is breathing. Let a small amount of give be felt, without pursuing it.\n【Working with MUNI Scent】\nPress a small amount of MUNI Scent into your palm, or open the bottle near your nose and take three easy breaths of it. Then rest a hand near your spine or a joint, and let scent and touch keep you company, without expecting anything to change.\nSmell is the only sense that skips rational analysis and reaches the centres of emotion and memory directly —\nlet the scent be a soft doorway, so the body can find flow inside its own discipline.",
      "awareness": "Body awareness here is not about hunting for what hurts,\nand not about making the body become something.\nIt's about choosing a part of the body that is relatively easy to feel,\nso attention has somewhere to rest.\nThis is not for the sake of breaking your principles,\nnor to change your standards.\nIt is simply keeping company with the experience that is happening.\nNo intervening, no correcting — letting awareness unfold on its own, once it's allowed to.",
