      "body": "【Emotional signature】\nRescue B is for the integration phase after an event, when the system begins to come down. You may no longer be in the chaos, and yet the aftershocks haven't settled — emotion, body and thought are still coming back into line. This isn't being stuck. It's a necessary transition, in which body and mind confirm that the danger has passed.\n【Through the lens of neuroception】\nWhat this card reflects: after an intense state, the body gradually stands down from alert and re-checks whether outside and inside now agree.\nIn this state, the body may show:\n* Breath becoming fuller, though it still needs time\n\n* Emotion surfacing occasionally, then receding on its own\n\n* A wish to be quiet rather than to act\n\nThis is not a problem. The system is completing its process of coming back.\n【How this essence supports you】\nThe support of Rescue B is in walking with the system through integration. It doesn't push action and doesn't ask for understanding. It lets the body slowly return everything that just happened to a place where it can be carried. When the inside is coherent again, the next step surfaces on its own.\n【Today's practice】\nFind a relatively quiet moment; sitting or lying down both work. Let your attention rest lightly on your whole body, or on the flow of your breath. There's no need to change the rhythm — just know that the body is breathing. Let \"it has passed\" be slowly felt by the body.\n【Working with MUNI Scent】\nPress a small amount of MUNI Scent into your palm, or open the bottle near your nose and take three easy breaths of it. Then rest a hand wherever in your body feels steadiest and most settled, and let scent and touch keep you company, without expecting anything to change.\nSmell is the only sense that skips rational analysis and reaches the centres of emotion and memory directly —\nlet the scent be a bridge through the transition, carrying the body whole from the event back to now.",
